Kings Mountain Mine Dewatering Successfully Completed 
Albemarle has successfully completed dewatering the Kings Mountain Mine open pit in North Carolina. The completion of dewatering marks a significant step forward for Albemarle’s long‑term plans at the site. As one of North America's largest hard-rock lithium deposits, the Kings Mountain mine has the
In The News
March 31, 2026
Insights in Lithium Chemistry: Shaping Advanced Rubber Materials 
Lithium chemistry is fundamental in producing advanced rubber materials that are durable, elastic and resilient. It enables precise polymer engineering, improving performance across various industries including mobility, infrastructure and specialty products.
Locations
February 20, 2025
Silver Peak Stands Alone as U.S. Lithium Resource 
Less than 2% of the world’s lithium production comes from the United States today, and almost all of that is sourced from Albemarle’s Silver Peak facility.
In The News
March 31, 2026
Grid Energy Storage 101: What It Is and Why It Matters 
Demand for stationary energy storage is surging as countries strengthen grids and support the energy transition, with output expected to jump in 2026. AI and data centers are accelerating electricity demand, and lithium-based batteries help balance peak loads, reduce outages, and delay grid upgrades

